Hmm — budget scale: FaCliHarness has a static `waitBudgetScale` getter. Top-level shutdownPty should default to the AMBIENT scale too (tests using it directly — tui_protype tearDown — should also scale on CI). Make it read the ambient env by default (like FaCliHarness.waitBudgetScale does) but accept an injection for unit tests... The helper spawns nothing itself — the poll loop with injectable clock would be over-enginering. Keep it simple: default scale = resolvePtyWaitBudgetScale(env). The repro test can pass budgetScale explicitly.

